    "text_full": "Skip to Content\n\nPagePlay\n\nGuides\nWhat is a CMS?\nLogging in\nLogging out\nWorking with pages\nWorking with paragraphs\nWorking with photos\nAdd downloadable files\nWorking with your Photobanner\nSite statistics (via Google Analytics)\nYour PagePlay email\nAdding new email accounts\nEmail account limit\nSetting up your email account\nArchiving your old emails\nReset an email account password\nSet an out of office message\nBuy a new domain\nShould you drop the www?\nAdding more users who can edit content\nSupported browsers\nUpdate your mail servers\nSearch engines\nWhy doesn't my site appear on Google?\nLink swapping & Search Engine Optimisation\nAvoiding ‘links’ pages\nSearch Engine Optimisation tips\nGoogle Search console Verification\nFacebook Like Box / Button\nOpening links in new tabs/windows\nReferrer terms and conditions\nSearch engines\nDoing well with search.\n\nPagePlay has been created to make the most of all of your content and ensure it's used in a way where ithe default is to be search engine friendly. There are however, some other ways that you can help to make sure you lift your site as high as it can be in the search rankings.\n\nRegularly adding original content to your site is the first. Creating interesting relevant articles or pages which are useful for your visitors will also be seen in a positive light by search engines.\n\nUse short headings and subheadings which include the most relevent and useful works for that page. Break long pages or articles into sections using headings.\n\nOften breaking a very long page down into several pages of 5 or more paragraphs which contain more specific topics will be more helpful for visitors and therefore seen positively by search engines.\n\nOther search questions...\n\nWhy isn't my site on Google?\n\nCan swapping links help my search ranking?\n\nWhy should I avoid links pages?\n\nhelp@pageplay.com\n\n© PagePlay Limited, 2026 - Simple Content Management by PagePlay\n\nCookie policy"
